662</lpage><article-title>A national study of neighborhood safety, outdoor play, television viewing, and obesity in preschool children</article-title><source>Pediatrics</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16140705</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carver</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Salmon</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Campbell</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Baur</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Garnett</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Crawford</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><volume>20</volume><issue>2</issue><year>2005</year><fpage>139</fpage><lpage>147</lpage><article-title>How do perceptions of local neighborhoods relate to adolescents' walking and cycling?</article-title><source>Am J Health Promot </source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16295706</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carver</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Timperio</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Crawford</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><volume>14</volume><issue>2</issue><year>2008</year><fpage>217</fpage><lpage>227</lpage><article-title>Playing it safe: the influence of neighbourhood safety on children's physical activity. A review</article-title><source>Health Place</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17662638</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><year>2002</year><publisher-loc>Atlanta (GA)</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</publisher-name><source>National Center for Injury Prevention and Control. CDC injury r